## Autonomous vault (default)

After substantive work — **without asking** "save to Obsidian?":

1. Search for existing project/topic note
2. Update or create in logical folder; tags + wikilinks
3. Log one line in `ai-tracking/` or daily note
4. End user reply with 1 line: what changed in vault

**Ask once only:** mass delete (>3 files), notes with backlinks, `Archive/`.

**Auto-delete OK:** empty stubs, `_draft/` junk, merged duplicates.

If Obsidian offline — note once, catch up when available.

**Not for vault:** `user-memory` (long notes), parallel web search tools.
